.TH P256TEST 1
.SH NAME
p256test \- test NIST P-256 ECDSA and ECDH
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B p256test
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B P256test
checks
.IR p256 (2)
against vectors from an independent library (Python's
.BR cryptography ),
offline:
.IP \(bu
a real ECDSA signature over a known message with a known key must
verify;
.IP \(bu
the same signature with one bit flipped must
.I not
verify, and the same against a one-bit-changed hash must
.I not
verify \(em an automated negative control (unlike most in this tree,
it can be automated, since a wrong signature is a safe computation,
not a memory hazard);
.IP \(bu
an ECDH shared secret with a known private scalar and known peer
point must equal the library's, and two freshly generated keypairs
must agree after exchange;
.IP \(bu
a point not on the curve must be rejected, both by
.B oncurve
and as an ECDH peer.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/p256test.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR p256 (2),
.IR tls12 (2)
.SH BUGS
Coverage is verify/agreement over the fixed vectors above plus a
round trip; there is no signing to test (\c
.IR p256 (2)
does not sign). A further hand control \(em corrupting a curve
constant, which must break every operation \(em is run by editing the
source.
